1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,263
A farmer grows more rice.

2
00:00:02,263 --> 00:00:03,915
A doctor treats cancer.

3
00:00:03,915 --> 00:00:06,865
A thin glass thread
carries your video call.

4
00:00:07,265 --> 00:00:09,150
Three very different stories.

5
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,647
But one science sits behind all three.

6
00:00:12,097 --> 00:00:14,190
Diya sees it in her own kitchen.

7
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:17,215
Salt, soap, a steel
cooker, a medicine strip.

8
00:00:17,565 --> 00:00:20,732
Every one of them comes to us
with the help of chemistry.

9
00:00:21,232 --> 00:00:25,352
By the end of this video, you will
see how chemists turn plain air into

10
00:00:25,352 --> 00:00:26,454
food for plants.

11
00:00:27,104 --> 00:00:28,510
So what is chemistry?

12
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:30,556
Chemistry studies matter.

13
00:00:30,556 --> 00:00:34,041
Matter is anything that has
mass and takes up space.

14
00:00:34,391 --> 00:00:38,076
Chemists ask what it is made of,
and how its parts are arranged.

15
00:00:38,426 --> 00:00:41,651
How it behaves, and how it
changes into something new.

16
00:00:42,251 --> 00:00:43,357
Take water.

17
00:00:43,357 --> 00:00:46,565
Two hydrogen atoms join one oxygen atom.

18
00:00:46,965 --> 00:00:50,112
Each puts in one electron,
and they share the pair.

19
00:00:50,112 --> 00:00:51,874
That shared pair is a bond.

20
00:00:52,524 --> 00:00:55,806
The chemist Roald Hoffmann
said it in one line.

21
00:00:55,806 --> 00:00:59,976
Chemistry is the science of
molecules and their transformations.

22
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:01,889
Transformation means change.

23
00:01:02,539 --> 00:01:05,522
Let's watch one change
on our molecule bench.

24
00:01:05,522 --> 00:01:08,138
The air around you is mostly nitrogen.

25
00:01:08,488 --> 00:01:13,756
Each nitrogen molecule is two nitrogen
atoms, locked by three shared pairs

26
00:01:13,756 --> 00:01:14,932
of electrons.

27
00:01:14,932 --> 00:01:16,235
A triple bond.

28
00:01:16,635 --> 00:01:20,356
Plants need nitrogen, but most
cannot take it from the air.

29
00:01:20,356 --> 00:01:22,339
The triple bond is too strong.

30
00:01:22,739 --> 00:01:26,775
So factories join nitrogen
with hydrogen to make ammonia.

31
00:01:26,775 --> 00:01:30,135
Ammonia is used to make
fertilisers like urea.

32
00:01:30,535 --> 00:01:31,435
Watch.

33
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:34,957
The old bonds break, the atoms
move, and new bonds form.

34
00:01:35,357 --> 00:01:40,918
Each ammonia molecule is one nitrogen
atom holding three hydrogen atoms.

35
00:01:41,568 --> 00:01:43,190
Now look at the counter.

36
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:45,331
On the left, two nitrogen atoms.

37
00:01:45,331 --> 00:01:47,000
On the right, only one.

38
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,643
Pause and think.

39
00:01:48,643 --> 00:01:53,050
Is nitrogen plus hydrogen gives
ammonia balanced, as it is written?

40
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:57,150
No!

41
00:01:56,708 --> 00:02:00,092
Two nitrogens on the left,
only one on the right.

42
00:02:00,092 --> 00:02:02,441
Atoms cannot just vanish or appear.

43
00:02:03,091 --> 00:02:05,373
Let's balance it, one step at a time.

44
00:02:05,723 --> 00:02:06,623
Step one.

45
00:02:06,527 --> 00:02:08,791
Atoms are never made or destroyed.

46
00:02:08,791 --> 00:02:12,183
So every atom on the left
must appear on the right.

47
00:02:12,933 --> 00:02:13,833
Step two.

48
00:02:13,805 --> 00:02:14,890
Fix nitrogen.

49
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:17,198
Put a two in front of ammonia.

50
00:02:17,198 --> 00:02:19,495
Now two nitrogens on each side.

51
00:02:20,245 --> 00:02:21,195
Step three.

52
00:02:21,195 --> 00:02:23,416
Two ammonias hold six hydrogens.

53
00:02:23,416 --> 00:02:26,029
So put a three in front of hydrogen.

54
00:02:26,779 --> 00:02:27,700
Step four.

55
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,726
Count again.

56
00:02:28,726 --> 00:02:30,514
Nitrogen, two and two.

57
00:02:30,514 --> 00:02:32,303
Hydrogen, six and six.

58
00:02:32,303 --> 00:02:33,203
Balanced.

59
00:02:33,857 --> 00:02:35,042
Remember this.

60
00:02:35,042 --> 00:02:37,423
Chemistry never makes new atoms.

61
00:02:37,423 --> 00:02:39,294
It only rearranges them.

62
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:41,730
Now, one worked example.

63
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:44,883
A nitrogen atom has a mass of fourteen u.

64
00:02:44,883 --> 00:02:46,220
Hydrogen, one u.

65
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:48,822
u is the unit for the mass of atoms.

66
00:02:49,322 --> 00:02:53,039
How much ammonia comes from
twenty eight grams of nitrogen?

67
00:02:53,539 --> 00:02:54,474
Left side.

68
00:02:54,474 --> 00:02:58,876
One nitrogen molecule, two times
fourteen, is twenty eight u.

69
00:02:58,876 --> 00:03:02,785
Three hydrogen molecules,
three times two, are six u.

70
00:03:03,535 --> 00:03:04,490
Right side.

71
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:07,998
One ammonia, fourteen plus
three, is seventeen u.

72
00:03:07,998 --> 00:03:10,292
Two ammonias make thirty four u.

73
00:03:11,042 --> 00:03:13,528
Twenty eight plus six is thirty four.

74
00:03:13,528 --> 00:03:15,660
The mass on both sides matches.

75
00:03:16,410 --> 00:03:18,442
Grams follow the same ratio.

76
00:03:18,442 --> 00:03:23,048
So twenty eight grams of nitrogen
gives thirty four grams of ammonia.

77
00:03:23,698 --> 00:03:26,220
Chemistry reaches far beyond farms.

78
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,120
Health.

79
00:03:26,944 --> 00:03:31,232
Chemists isolate drugs from
nature and make them in the lab.

80
00:03:31,232 --> 00:03:33,644
Cisplatin and taxol treat cancer.

81
00:03:33,644 --> 00:03:35,739
AZT helps AIDS patients.

82
00:03:36,139 --> 00:03:37,039
Food.

83
00:03:36,790 --> 00:03:41,071
Fertilisers like urea, and
pesticides that protect crops.

84
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:42,598
New materials.

85
00:03:42,598 --> 00:03:47,056
Superconducting ceramics, conducting
polymers, and optical fibres that

86
00:03:47,056 --> 00:03:48,079
carry light.

87
00:03:48,479 --> 00:03:49,379
Industry.

88
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:53,893
Acids, alkalis, salts, dyes,
polymers, soaps and detergents.

89
00:03:53,893 --> 00:03:56,845
The factories that make them create jobs.

90
00:03:57,245 --> 00:03:58,296
Environment.

91
00:03:58,296 --> 00:04:03,645
Chemists made safer replacements for
CF Cs, the fridge gases that damaged

92
00:04:03,645 --> 00:04:05,066
the ozone layer.

93
00:04:05,466 --> 00:04:10,074
Big problems remain, like controlling
greenhouse gases such as methane

94
00:04:10,074 --> 00:04:11,570
and carbon dioxide.

95
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:13,685
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:14,035 --> 00:04:17,153
Some students balance by
changing the small numbers.

97
00:04:17,153 --> 00:04:19,998
They write H three,
instead of three H two.

98
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:23,096
But that changes the substance itself.

99
00:04:23,096 --> 00:04:24,869
H two is hydrogen gas.

100
00:04:24,869 --> 00:04:26,202
H three is not.

101
00:04:26,202 --> 00:04:28,910
Only change the big numbers in front.

102
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,075
Where is this asked?

103
00:04:31,075 --> 00:04:34,470
As short recall questions
on the uses of chemistry.

104
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:37,804
And balancing comes back
in almost every numerical.

105
00:04:38,404 --> 00:04:39,757
Exam level now.

106
00:04:39,757 --> 00:04:45,226
Fifty six grams of nitrogen reacts
completely with hydrogen to form ammonia.

107
00:04:45,226 --> 00:04:47,405
What mass of ammonia forms?

108
00:04:47,405 --> 00:04:48,815
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:54,215 --> 00:04:55,585
The answer is C.

110
00:04:55,585 --> 00:04:56,998
Sixty eight grams.

111
00:04:57,498 --> 00:05:01,736
From the balanced equation, twenty
eight grams of nitrogen gives thirty

112
00:05:01,736 --> 00:05:03,282
four grams of ammonia.

113
00:05:03,782 --> 00:05:05,893
Fifty six is twice twenty eight.

114
00:05:05,893 --> 00:05:09,427
So the ammonia is twice thirty
four, sixty eight grams.

115
00:05:09,927 --> 00:05:14,700
Check: it uses twelve grams of hydrogen,
and fifty six plus twelve is sixty

116
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:15,600
eight.

117
00:05:15,302 --> 00:05:17,886
B forgot that the hydrogen doubles too.

118
00:05:18,486 --> 00:05:19,948
Here is your recap.

119
00:05:19,948 --> 00:05:21,451
Screenshot this card.

120
00:05:24,651 --> 00:05:27,487
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

121
00:05:27,887 --> 00:05:28,787
One.

122
00:05:28,401 --> 00:05:31,971
Name two drugs that chemistry
gave to cancer treatment.

123
00:05:32,771 --> 00:05:33,671
Two.

124
00:05:33,324 --> 00:05:37,853
Why can't we balance an equation
by changing H two into H three?

125
00:05:38,653 --> 00:05:39,553
Three.

126
00:05:39,263 --> 00:05:43,550
Why must the total mass be the
same on both sides of a reaction?

127
00:05:44,450 --> 00:05:47,357
Next time: is air a compound or a mixture?

128
00:05:47,357 --> 00:05:50,604
We find out in nature and
classification of matter.
